      "shift": "23 Jan 2026, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "Let $S = \\{z: 3 \\le |2z-3(1+i)| \\le 7\\}$ be a set of complex numbers. Then $\\underset{z \\in S}{\\min} \\left| z + \\frac{1}{2}(5+3i) \\right|$ is equal to :",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$\\;\\frac{1}{2}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$\\;\\frac{5}{2}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "2",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$\\;\\frac{3}{2}$",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Rewrite the condition: $\\frac{3}{2} \\le \\left|z-\\frac{3}{2}(1+i)\\right| \\le \\frac{7}{2}$.\nSo $S$ is an annulus with centre $C\\left(\\frac32,\\frac32\\right)$, inner radius $\\frac32$ and outer radius $\\frac72$.\n$\\left|z+\\frac12(5+3i)\\right|$ is the distance of $z$ from $P\\left(-\\frac52,-\\frac32\\right)$.\n$CP=\\sqrt{4^2+3^2}=5$.\nSince $5>\\frac72$, $P$ lies outside the outer circle.\nThe minimum distance is $CP-\\frac72=5-\\frac72=\\frac32$.\nAnswer: (D) $\\frac32$"
    },
